  "term": "likelihood ratio",
  "definition": "A likelihood ratio is a statistical comparison, used in signal detection, of how probable an observed pattern is under one condition versus another. In this context, it helps classify brain-imaging findings by weighing whether they more closely match Alzheimer’s disease or normal control data.",
